IMPORT prelude

-- Ontario Taxation Act, 2007 (S.O. 2007, c. 11, Sched. A), Part II -- the Ontario personal income tax of an individual
-- resident in Ontario on the last day of the year with no income earned outside Ontario (s 4 (1) para 1), and three
-- benefits the Act pays to individuals: the Ontario child benefit (s 104) and the Ontario sales tax credit part of the
-- Ontario Trillium Benefit (s 103.8).
--
-- Encoded: liability (s 4 (1), (3)); the calculation steps (s 5 (1)); the rates (s 3 (1) definitions) and basic personal
-- income tax (s 6 (1)); the non-refundable credits in s 9 (2), (3), (4), (8), (9), (10), (12) (others an input in dollars of
-- credit); the Ontario surtax (s 16 (1), (2)); the Ontario tax reduction (s 20 (1)-(7), (9)); the low-income individuals
-- and families tax credit (LIFT, s 21.1 (1), (2), (3.1), (4)); the Ontario Health Premium (s 24 (0.1), (1), (2)); the
-- Ontario child benefit (s 104 (4), (5), (5.1), (6.2), (8), (9)); the Ontario sales tax credit (s 103.8 (2)-(4)).
--
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE. The dollar amounts that s 23 indexes each year are carried in a record, `Ontario amounts`; the
-- amounts written in the Act are `the amounts written in the Act`. The individual's questions are in on-pit-seat.l4.
--
-- The tax base is the individual's taxable income for the year (s 3 (1) "tax base" (a)), computed under the federal
-- Income Tax Act. It is an input here; see the federal encoding subjects/ca/income-tax-act/ (cross-folder IMPORT is not
-- possible in the stable l4).
--
-- Edition: e-Laws consolidation from 2026-07-01 to the e-Laws currency date 2026-10-14 (last amendment 2026, c. 2,
-- Sched. 15), deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/S.O.-2007-c.-11-Sched.-A.txt.
-- © King's Printer for Ontario, 2007. NOT AN OFFICIAL VERSION: the statutory words quoted in comments here are from an
-- unofficial reproduction of the consolidated law published on e-Laws; official copies are those described in the
-- Legislation Act, 2006.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Taxation Act, 2007 -- Ontario personal income tax and benefits of an individual`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `only an individual resident in Ontario on the last day of the year is encoded (s 4 (1) para 1)`
    `income earned outside Ontario brings in the Ontario allocation factor (s 4 (1) para 2, s 6 (2)), which is not encoded`
    `only the 2026 taxation year has deposited indexed amounts (T4127, January 2026)`
    `split income (s 12.1) is not encoded`
    `minimum tax (s 19.2) is not encoded`
    `the overseas employment and minimum tax carryover credits (ss 14, 15) are not encoded`
    `averaging and adjustments under subdivision f (ss 17 to 19) are not encoded`
    `the disability supplement for an individual under 18 (s 9 (12) (a)) is not encoded`
    `only benefit months from July 2026 to June 2027 have deposited indexed amounts`
    `the seniors' income threshold of s 103.8 (5) is not encoded`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `Arithmetic`

-- "the amount, if any, by which x exceeds y": never below zero.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the excess of` x `over` y MEANS max 0 (x MINUS y)

-- The part of a base that falls between two limits ("the amount by which the tax base exceeds lo and does not exceed hi").
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER, lo IS A NUMBER, hi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part of` base `between` lo `and` hi MEANS `the excess of` (min base hi) `over` lo

§§ `s 3 (1) -- the tax rates`

-- s 3 (1): "lowest tax rate" "(b) 5.05 per cent in respect of taxation years ending after December 31, 2009";
-- "second-lowest tax rate" means 9.15 per cent; "middle tax rate" means 11.16 per cent; "second-highest tax rate"
-- means 12.16 per cent; "highest tax rate" "(b) 13.16 per cent in respect of taxation years ending after December 31, 2012".
`the lowest tax rate`         MEANS 0.0505
`the second-lowest tax rate`  MEANS 0.0915
`the middle tax rate`         MEANS 0.1116
`the second-highest tax rate` MEANS 0.1216
`the highest tax rate`        MEANS 0.1316

§§ `s 23 -- the amounts indexed each year`

-- s 23 (1) lists the provisions whose dollar amounts "shall be adjusted in accordance with this section for every
-- taxation year": paragraphs 1 and 2 of s 6 (1) and paragraph 3 except $150,000 (para 1, 1.1); s 9 (2) to (6), (8),
-- (10), (11), (12) and (20) (para 2); the surtax thresholds in s 16 (1) (a) (ii) and (b) (ii) (para 4); s 20 (4) and (5)
-- (para 5). The adjustment uses the Ontario CPI (s 23 (2), (5)) and rounds to a whole dollar (s 23 (4)). The CPI figures
-- are not in the Act, so the adjusted amounts are carried here as a record. The $150,000 and $220,000 bracket limits and
-- the s 21.1 (LIFT) and s 24 (Health Premium) amounts are not listed in s 23 (1) and are fixed.
DECLARE `Ontario amounts` HAS
    `first bracket limit`            IS A NUMBER   -- s 6 (1) paras 1, 2: $40,120 as written
    `second bracket limit`           IS A NUMBER   -- s 6 (1) paras 2, 3: $80,242 as written
    `personal amount base`           IS A NUMBER   -- s 9 (2): $8,881 as written
    `spouse amount base`             IS A NUMBER   -- s 9 (3), (4): $7,541 as written
    `spouse income floor`            IS A NUMBER   -- s 9 (3), (4): $754 as written
    `age amount base`                IS A NUMBER   -- s 9 (8): $4,336 as written
    `age income threshold`           IS A NUMBER   -- s 9 (8): $32,280 as written
    `pension amount maximum`         IS A NUMBER   -- s 9 (10): $1,228 as written
    `impairment amount base`         IS A NUMBER   -- s 9 (12): $7,175 as written
    `first surtax threshold`         IS A NUMBER   -- s 16 (1) (a) (ii): $4,006 as written
    `second surtax threshold`        IS A NUMBER   -- s 16 (1) (b) (ii): $5,127 as written
    `basic reduction amount`         IS A NUMBER   -- s 20 (4): $205 as written
    `dependant reduction amount`     IS A NUMBER   -- s 20 (5): $379 as written

-- The figures as written in the deposited consolidation, before any s 23 adjustment.
`the amounts written in the Act` MEANS
    `Ontario amounts` WITH
        `first bracket limit`        IS 40120
        `second bracket limit`       IS 80242
        `personal amount base`       IS 8881
        `spouse amount base`         IS 7541
        `spouse income floor`        IS 754
        `age amount base`            IS 4336
        `age income threshold`       IS 32280
        `pension amount maximum`     IS 1228
        `impairment amount base`     IS 7175
        `first surtax threshold`     IS 4006
        `second surtax threshold`    IS 5127
        `basic reduction amount`     IS 205
        `dependant reduction amount` IS 379

§§ `s 4 (1) -- who is liable, and which case is encoded`

-- s 4 (1): "The following individuals shall pay taxes in accordance with this Part ...: 1. Every individual who is
-- resident in Ontario on the last day of the year and who has no income earned outside Ontario for the year. 2. Every
-- individual who is resident in Ontario on the last day of the year and who has income earned outside Ontario for the
-- year. 3. Every individual who is not resident in Ontario on the last day of the year but who has income earned in
-- Ontario for the year."
DECLARE `Liability under s 4 (1)` IS ONE OF
    `paragraph 1 -- resident on the last day, no income earned outside Ontario`
    `paragraph 2 -- resident on the last day, with income earned outside Ontario`
    `paragraph 3 -- not resident on the last day, with income earned in Ontario`
    `not liable under s 4 (1)`

GIVEN `resident in Ontario on the last day of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has income earned outside Ontario` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has income earned in Ontario` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Liability under s 4 (1)`
`the s 4 (1) paragraph that applies` MEANS
    IF `resident in Ontario on the last day of the year`
    THEN IF `has income earned outside Ontario`
         THEN `paragraph 2 -- resident on the last day, with income earned outside Ontario`
         ELSE `paragraph 1 -- resident on the last day, no income earned outside Ontario`
    ELSE IF `has income earned in Ontario`
         THEN `paragraph 3 -- not resident on the last day, with income earned in Ontario`
         ELSE `not liable under s 4 (1)`

§§ `s 6 (1) -- basic personal income tax`

-- s 6 (1): the lowest rate on the tax base "that does not exceed $40,120"; the second-lowest rate on the amount over
-- $40,120 and not over $80,242; the middle rate over $80,242 and not over $150,000; the second-highest rate over $150,000
-- and not over $220,000; the highest rate over $220,000. The two lower limits are indexed (s 23 (1) paras 1, 1.1).
GIVEN `amounts` IS AN `Ontario amounts`, `tax base` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic personal income tax` MEANS
        (`the lowest tax rate`         TIMES (`the part of` `tax base` `between` 0 `and` (`amounts`'s `first bracket limit`)))
    PLUS (`the second-lowest tax rate` TIMES (`the part of` `tax base` `between` (`amounts`'s `first bracket limit`) `and` (`amounts`'s `second bracket limit`)))
    PLUS (`the middle tax rate`        TIMES (`the part of` `tax base` `between` (`amounts`'s `second bracket limit`) `and` 150000))
    PLUS (`the second-highest tax rate` TIMES (`the part of` `tax base` `between` 150000 `and` 220000))
    PLUS (`the highest tax rate`       TIMES (`the excess of` `tax base` `over` 220000))

§§ `s 9 -- non-refundable tax credits`

-- s 9 (2): "calculated by multiplying the lowest tax rate for the year by $8,881", if entitled to a deduction under
-- paragraph 118 (1) (a), (b) or (c) of the Federal Act (a borrowed term, asked as a fact).
GIVEN `amounts` IS AN `Ontario amounts`, `entitled under ITA 118 (1) (a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the personal tax credit` MEANS
    IF `entitled under ITA 118 (1) (a), (b) or (c)`
    THEN `the lowest tax rate` TIMES (`amounts`'s `personal amount base`)
    ELSE 0

-- s 9 (3): "A × [$7,541 – (B – $754)]", "B" being "the greater of $754 and the income for the year of the individual's
-- spouse or common-law partner". s 9 (4) is the same formula for a wholly dependent person, "C" being the greater of $754
-- and that person's income. The Act does not say "if any"; a negative result is read as no credit.
GIVEN `amounts` IS AN `Ontario amounts`, `the other person's income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the spouse or wholly dependent person formula` MEANS
    LET `B` MEANS (max (`amounts`'s `spouse income floor`) `the other person's income`) MINUS (`amounts`'s `spouse income floor`)
    IN  `the lowest tax rate` TIMES (`the excess of` (`amounts`'s `spouse amount base`) `over` `B`)

GIVEN `amounts` IS AN `Ontario amounts`
      `entitled under ITA 118 (1) (a) for a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `spouse's income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax credit for spouse or common-law partner` MEANS
    IF `entitled under ITA 118 (1) (a) for a spouse`
    THEN `the spouse or wholly dependent person formula` `amounts` `spouse's income`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `amounts` IS AN `Ontario amounts`
      `entitled under ITA 118 (1) (b) for a wholly dependent person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `dependant's income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax credit for wholly dependent person` MEANS
    IF `entitled under ITA 118 (1) (b) for a wholly dependent person`
    THEN `the spouse or wholly dependent person formula` `amounts` `dependant's income`
    ELSE 0

-- s 9 (8): "A × ($4,336 – H)", "H" being "15 per cent of the amount, if any, by which the individual's income for the
-- year would exceed $32,280" (leaving out s 79 gains and s 20 (1) (ww) deductions, which the income figure is asked net of).
GIVEN `amounts` IS AN `Ontario amounts`
      `entitled under ITA 118 (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `income for the age credit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age tax credit` MEANS
    IF `entitled under ITA 118 (2)`
    THEN LET `H` MEANS 0.15 TIMES (`the excess of` `income for the age credit` `over` (`amounts`'s `age income threshold`))
         IN  `the lowest tax rate` TIMES (`the excess of` (`amounts`'s `age amount base`) `over` `H`)
    ELSE 0

-- s 9 (9): the amount "that would be determined ... under section 118.7 of the Federal Act if the reference in that
-- section to the appropriate percentage were read as a reference to the lowest tax rate". The s 118.7 base (the EI
-- premiums and CPP contributions that section counts) is asked as a fact.
GIVEN `the ITA 118.7 premiums and contributions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax credit for EI premiums and CPP contributions` MEANS
    `the lowest tax rate` TIMES `the ITA 118.7 premiums and contributions`

-- s 9 (10): "A × I", "I" being "the lesser of $1,228 and" the eligible pension income (and the s 118 (3) "B" amounts).
GIVEN `amounts` IS AN `Ontario amounts`
      `entitled under ITA 118 (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `eligible pension income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pension tax credit` MEANS
    IF `entitled under ITA 118 (3)`
    THEN `the lowest tax rate` TIMES (min (`amounts`'s `pension amount maximum`) `eligible pension income`)
    ELSE 0

-- s 9 (12): "A × ($7,175 + M)", "M" being, for an individual under 18 at the end of the year, a supplement, and "(b) in
-- any other case, nil". The supplement is an input here (the seat covers adults only).
GIVEN `amounts` IS AN `Ontario amounts`
      `entitled under ITA 118.3 (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the under-18 supplement M` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the mental or physical impairment tax credit` MEANS
    IF `entitled under ITA 118.3 (1)`
    THEN `the lowest tax rate` TIMES ((`amounts`'s `impairment amount base`) PLUS `the under-18 supplement M`)
    ELSE 0

-- The facts the s 9 credits read.
DECLARE `Credit facts` HAS
    `entitled to the basic personal deduction`       IS A BOOLEAN  -- ITA 118 (1) (a), (b) or (c)
    `claims for a spouse`                            IS A BOOLEAN  -- ITA 118 (1) (a)
    `income of the spouse`                           IS A NUMBER
    `claims for a wholly dependent person`           IS A BOOLEAN  -- ITA 118 (1) (b)
    `income of the wholly dependent person`          IS A NUMBER
    `entitled to the age deduction`                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- ITA 118 (2): 65 or older at year end
    `net income for the age credit`                  IS A NUMBER
    `CPP contributions and EI premiums under 118.7`  IS A NUMBER
    `entitled to the pension deduction`              IS A BOOLEAN  -- ITA 118 (3)
    `pension income for the credit`                  IS A NUMBER
    `entitled to the disability deduction`           IS A BOOLEAN  -- ITA 118.3 (1)
    `impairment supplement`                          IS A NUMBER   -- s 9 (12) "M"; nil for an adult
    `other Ontario non-refundable credits`           IS A NUMBER   -- dollars of credit under the rest of s 9

-- s 9 (1) with s 8: the sum of the credits the individual is entitled to and deducts.
GIVEN `amounts` IS AN `Ontario amounts`, `facts` IS A `Credit facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the non-refundable tax credits` MEANS
         `the personal tax credit` `amounts` (`facts`'s `entitled to the basic personal deduction`)
    PLUS `the tax credit for spouse or common-law partner` `amounts` (`facts`'s `claims for a spouse`) (`facts`'s `income of the spouse`)
    PLUS `the tax credit for wholly dependent person` `amounts` (`facts`'s `claims for a wholly dependent person`) (`facts`'s `income of the wholly dependent person`)
    PLUS `the age tax credit` `amounts` (`facts`'s `entitled to the age deduction`) (`facts`'s `net income for the age credit`)
    PLUS `the tax credit for EI premiums and CPP contributions` (`facts`'s `CPP contributions and EI premiums under 118.7`)
    PLUS `the pension tax credit` `amounts` (`facts`'s `entitled to the pension deduction`) (`facts`'s `pension income for the credit`)
    PLUS `the mental or physical impairment tax credit` `amounts` (`facts`'s `entitled to the disability deduction`) (`facts`'s `impairment supplement`)
    PLUS `facts`'s `other Ontario non-refundable credits`

§§ `s 16 -- the Ontario surtax`

-- s 16 (2): the gross tax amount is basic personal income tax less the subdivision b credits ("the amount, if any"), plus
-- additional tax under ss 11 and 12 (none for a taxation year after 2015), less the subdivision d credits.
GIVEN `basic tax` IS A NUMBER, `non-refundable credits` IS A NUMBER, `subdivision d credits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the gross tax amount` MEANS
    `the excess of` (`the excess of` `basic tax` `over` `non-refundable credits`) `over` `subdivision d credits`

-- s 16 (1): "(a) 20 per cent of the amount, if any, by which the gross tax amount ... exceeds ... (ii) $4,006 ...; and
-- (b) 36 per cent of the amount, if any, by which the gross tax amount ... exceeds ... (ii) $5,127". Both indexed.
GIVEN `amounts` IS AN `Ontario amounts`, `gross tax amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Ontario surtax` MEANS
         (0.20 TIMES (`the excess of` `gross tax amount` `over` (`amounts`'s `first surtax threshold`)))
    PLUS (0.36 TIMES (`the excess of` `gross tax amount` `over` (`amounts`'s `second surtax threshold`)))

§§ `s 20 -- the Ontario tax reduction`

-- s 20 (3): personal amount = A + B + C: the basic reduction (s 20 (4): $205 times the Ontario allocation factor, which is
-- 1 for a paragraph 1 individual), plus the eligible amount (s 20 (5): $379) for each dependant under 18 and for each
-- dependant with a mental or physical infirmity that the individual may include.
-- s 20 (2): where the individual "resides with a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on December 31" an amount for a
-- dependant may be included only "if the individual's income for the year exceeds the income of the cohabiting spouse".
-- s 20 (6), (7) say which dependants count (the CCB eligible individual; no one else having claimed); asked as counts.
GIVEN `amounts` IS AN `Ontario amounts`
      `dependants under 18 the individual may include` IS A NUMBER
      `infirm dependants the individual may include` IS A NUMBER
      `resides with a cohabiting spouse on December 31` IS A BOOLEAN
      `individual's income` IS A NUMBER
      `cohabiting spouse's income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the personal amount for the tax reduction` MEANS
    LET `may include dependants` MEANS
            (NOT `resides with a cohabiting spouse on December 31`)
         OR `individual's income` GREATER THAN `cohabiting spouse's income`
    IN  (`amounts`'s `basic reduction amount`)
        PLUS (IF `may include dependants`
              THEN (`amounts`'s `dependant reduction amount`) TIMES
                       (`dependants under 18 the individual may include` PLUS `infirm dependants the individual may include`)
              ELSE 0)

-- s 20 (9): no reduction if (a) federal tax is under Division E.1 (minimum tax, not encoded); (b) not resident in Canada
-- at the beginning of the year; (c) not resident in Canada at any time in the calendar year; (d) not resident in Ontario
-- on the last day; (e) a bankrupt at any time in the calendar year; (f) a return filed by a trustee in bankruptcy;
-- (g) a trust.
GIVEN `resident in Canada at the beginning of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `resident in Canada at some time in the calendar year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `resident in Ontario on the last day of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `bankrupt at any time in the calendar year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `return filed by a trustee in bankruptcy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 20 (9) exception applies` IF
        (NOT `resident in Canada at the beginning of the year`)
    OR  (NOT `resident in Canada at some time in the calendar year`)
    OR  (NOT `resident in Ontario on the last day of the year`)
    OR  `bankrupt at any time in the calendar year`
    OR  `return filed by a trustee in bankruptcy`

-- s 20 (1): "a tax credit equal to the amount, if any, by which twice the individual's personal amount for the year
-- exceeds the amount of tax otherwise payable", "tax otherwise payable" being the tax without ss 20, 21, 21.1 and 22
-- (s 20 (10)).
GIVEN `personal amount` IS A NUMBER, `tax otherwise payable` IS A NUMBER, `excepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Ontario tax reduction` MEANS
    IF `excepted`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the excess of` (2 TIMES `personal amount`) `over` `tax otherwise payable`

§§ `s 21.1 -- the low-income individuals and families tax credit (LIFT)`

-- s 21.1 (1), (2): eligible if resident in Canada at the beginning of the year, unless (a) not resident in Ontario on the
-- last day; (b) not resident in Canada at any time in the calendar year; (c) a trust; (d) minimum tax; (e) a bankrupt in
-- the calendar year; (f) a return filed by a trustee in bankruptcy; (g) "confined to a prison or similar institution for
-- a period that includes December 31 of the previous taxation year and the first 179 days in the taxation year".
GIVEN `resident in Canada at the beginning of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `resident in Canada at some time in the calendar year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `resident in Ontario on the last day of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `bankrupt at any time in the calendar year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `return filed by a trustee in bankruptcy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `confined to a prison from December 31 through the first 179 days` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an eligible individual for LIFT` IF
        `resident in Canada at the beginning of the year`
    AND `resident in Ontario on the last day of the year`
    AND `resident in Canada at some time in the calendar year`
    AND (NOT `bankrupt at any time in the calendar year`)
    AND (NOT `return filed by a trustee in bankruptcy`)
    AND (NOT `confined to a prison from December 31 through the first 179 days`)

-- s 21.1 (3.1): "(D – E) × F", "D" the lesser of $875 and the lowest tax rate times employment income; "E" 5 per cent of
-- the greater of the excess of personal adjusted income over $32,500 and the excess of adjusted income over $65,000; "F"
-- the Ontario allocation factor (1 here). A negative (D - E) is read as no credit.
GIVEN `eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `employment income` IS A NUMBER
      `personal adjusted income` IS A NUMBER
      `adjusted income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the LIFT credit` MEANS
    IF `eligible`
    THEN LET `D` MEANS min 875 (`the lowest tax rate` TIMES `employment income`)
             `E` MEANS 0.05 TIMES (max (`the excess of` `personal adjusted income` `over` 32500) (`the excess of` `adjusted income` `over` 65000))
         IN  `the excess of` `D` `over` `E`
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 5 (1) -- the personal income tax payable under Division B`

DECLARE `Tax facts` HAS
    `tax base`                       IS A NUMBER  -- s 3 (1): taxable income for the year (federal)
    `credits`                        IS A `Credit facts`
    `subdivision d credit amount`    IS A NUMBER  -- ss 14, 15
    `Ontario dividend tax credit`    IS A NUMBER  -- s 19.1, subdivision g
    `Ontario foreign tax credit`     IS A NUMBER  -- s 21, subdivision i
    `under-18 dependants counted`    IS A NUMBER  -- s 20 (3) "B"
    `infirm dependants counted`      IS A NUMBER  -- s 20 (3) "C"
    `cohabiting spouse on December 31` IS A BOOLEAN
    `individual's net income`        IS A NUMBER  -- s 20 (2) "income"
    `spouse's net income`            IS A NUMBER
    `tax reduction excepted`         IS A BOOLEAN -- s 20 (9)
    `LIFT eligible`                  IS A BOOLEAN -- s 21.1 (1), (2)
    `employment income`              IS A NUMBER  -- s 21.1 (4)
    `personal adjusted income`       IS A NUMBER  -- s 21.1 (4)
    `adjusted income`                IS A NUMBER  -- s 21.1 (4)

-- s 5 (1), paragraphs 1 to 7 (subdivisions c, f and h nil in the case encoded): the "tax otherwise payable" of s 20 (10).
GIVEN `amounts` IS AN `Ontario amounts`, `facts` IS A `Tax facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax before subdivision i credits` MEANS
    LET `basic`      MEANS `the basic personal income tax` `amounts` (`facts`'s `tax base`)
        `nrtc`       MEANS `the non-refundable tax credits` `amounts` (`facts`'s `credits`)
        `paragraph 4` MEANS `the gross tax amount` `basic` `nrtc` (`facts`'s `subdivision d credit amount`)
        `paragraph 5` MEANS `paragraph 4` PLUS (`the Ontario surtax` `amounts` `paragraph 4`)
    IN  `the excess of` `paragraph 5` `over` (`facts`'s `Ontario dividend tax credit`)

-- s 5 (1) para 8: the tax payable is "the amount, if any, by which the total determined under paragraph 7 exceeds the sum
-- of all tax credits under subdivision i" (ss 20, 21, 21.1, 22).
GIVEN `amounts` IS AN `Ontario amounts`, `facts` IS A `Tax facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the personal income tax payable under Division B` MEANS
    LET `paragraph 7` MEANS `the tax before subdivision i credits` `amounts` `facts`
        `personal amount` MEANS `the personal amount for the tax reduction` `amounts`
                                   (`facts`'s `under-18 dependants counted`) (`facts`'s `infirm dependants counted`)
                                   (`facts`'s `cohabiting spouse on December 31`) (`facts`'s `individual's net income`) (`facts`'s `spouse's net income`)
        `reduction` MEANS `the Ontario tax reduction` `personal amount` `paragraph 7` (`facts`'s `tax reduction excepted`)
        `lift` MEANS `the LIFT credit` (`facts`'s `LIFT eligible`) (`facts`'s `employment income`) (`facts`'s `personal adjusted income`) (`facts`'s `adjusted income`)
    IN  `the excess of` `paragraph 7` `over` (`reduction` PLUS (`facts`'s `Ontario foreign tax credit`) PLUS `lift`)

§§ `s 24 -- the Ontario Health Premium`

-- s 24 (0.1): combined income = taxable income + split income (nil where s 12.1 does not apply).
-- s 24 (2): nil up to $20,000; 0.06 × the lesser of $5,000 and the excess over $20,000 (to $36,000); $300 + 0.06 × the
-- lesser of $2,500 and the excess over $36,000 (to $48,000); $450 + 0.25 × the lesser of $600 and the excess over $48,000
-- (to $72,000); $600 + 0.25 × the lesser of $600 and the excess over $72,000 (to $200,000); $750 + 0.25 × the lesser of
-- $600 and the excess over $200,000. None of these amounts is indexed.
GIVEN `combined income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Ontario Health Premium` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `combined income` AT MOST 20000  THEN 0
        IF `combined income` AT MOST 36000  THEN 0.06 TIMES (min 5000 (`combined income` MINUS 20000))
        IF `combined income` AT MOST 48000  THEN 300 PLUS (0.06 TIMES (min 2500 (`combined income` MINUS 36000)))
        IF `combined income` AT MOST 72000  THEN 450 PLUS (0.25 TIMES (min 600 (`combined income` MINUS 48000)))
        IF `combined income` AT MOST 200000 THEN 600 PLUS (0.25 TIMES (min 600 (`combined income` MINUS 72000)))
        OTHERWISE 750 PLUS (0.25 TIMES (min 600 (`combined income` MINUS 200000)))

-- s 24 (1): the premium is payable by an individual described in paragraph 1 or 2 of s 4 (1); (3): not by a trust.
GIVEN `liability` IS A `Liability under s 4 (1)`, `combined income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Ontario Health Premium payable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `liability`
    WHEN `paragraph 1 -- resident on the last day, no income earned outside Ontario` THEN `the Ontario Health Premium` `combined income`
    WHEN `paragraph 2 -- resident on the last day, with income earned outside Ontario` THEN `the Ontario Health Premium` `combined income`
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 4 (3): "An individual's tax payable under this Part ... is the sum of, (a) the individual's tax payable under
-- Division B for the year; and (b) the individual's tax payable under Division C for the year."
GIVEN `Division B tax` IS A NUMBER, `Division C premium` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax payable under Part II` MEANS `Division B tax` PLUS `Division C premium`

§§ `s 104 -- the Ontario child benefit`

-- s 104 (4): an overpayment (the benefit) arises for a month if "1. The individual is an eligible individual at the
-- beginning of the month in respect of one or more qualified dependants and is entitled to receive a Canada child benefit
-- for that month. 2. The individual is resident in Ontario on the first day of the month. 3. The individual and, if
-- required by the Ontario Minister, the person who is the individual's cohabiting spouse or common-law partner have each
-- filed a return of income for the base taxation year."
GIVEN `eligible individual for one or more qualified dependants at the beginning of the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `entitled to a Canada child benefit for the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `resident in Ontario on the first day of the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `returns filed for the base taxation year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 104 (4) conditions are met` IF
        `eligible individual for one or more qualified dependants at the beginning of the month`
    AND `entitled to a Canada child benefit for the month`
    AND `resident in Ontario on the first day of the month`
    AND `returns filed for the base taxation year`

-- The two s 104 (5) amounts that s 23 (3.5) indexes: "A" (d) $1,310 a child, and the $20,000 in "C".
DECLARE `OCB amounts` HAS
    `amount per qualified dependant` IS A NUMBER
    `income threshold`               IS A NUMBER

`the OCB amounts written in the Act` MEANS
    `OCB amounts` WITH
        `amount per qualified dependant` IS 1310
        `income threshold`               IS 20000

-- s 104 (5): "[(A × B) – C]/12", "B" the number of qualified dependants, "C" "8 per cent of the amount, if any, by which
-- the individual's adjusted income for the base taxation year ... exceeds $20,000". A negative result is read as nil.
GIVEN `ocb` IS AN `OCB amounts`, `qualified dependants` IS A NUMBER, `adjusted income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 104 (5) monthly amount` MEANS
    LET `A times B` MEANS (`ocb`'s `amount per qualified dependant`) TIMES `qualified dependants`
        `C` MEANS 0.08 TIMES (`the excess of` `adjusted income` `over` (`ocb`'s `income threshold`))
    IN  (`the excess of` `A times B` `over` `C`) DIVIDED BY 12

-- s 104 (5.1): a shared-custody parent gets "(A + B)/2", A the s (5) amount, B the s (5) amount "as if the individual
-- were not an eligible individual in respect of any qualified dependants in respect of whom the individual is a
-- shared-custody parent". s 104 (6.2): if the total for the 12-month period from July "is less than $2.01", it is nil
-- (the monthly amount is treated as constant over the period).
GIVEN `ocb` IS AN `OCB amounts`
      `conditions met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `qualified dependants` IS A NUMBER
      `of whom in shared custody` IS A NUMBER
      `adjusted income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Ontario child benefit for the month` MEANS
    IF (NOT `conditions met`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE LET `full` MEANS `the s 104 (5) monthly amount` `ocb` `qualified dependants` `adjusted income`
             `without shared` MEANS `the s 104 (5) monthly amount` `ocb` (`qualified dependants` MINUS `of whom in shared custody`) `adjusted income`
             `monthly` MEANS IF `of whom in shared custody` GREATER THAN 0
                             THEN (`full` PLUS `without shared`) DIVIDED BY 2
                             ELSE `full`
         IN  IF (`monthly` TIMES 12) LESS THAN 2.01 THEN 0 ELSE `monthly`

§§ `s 103.8 -- the Ontario sales tax credit (part of the Ontario Trillium Benefit, s 103.3)`

-- s 103.8 (2): eligible for a month if "1. At the beginning of the month, the individual is resident in Ontario. 2. At the
-- beginning of the month, the individual is an eligible individual as defined in subsection 122.5 (1) of the Federal Act
-- and is not excluded ... because of subsection 122.5 (2) ... 3. The individual and, if required by the Ontario Minister,
-- the person who is the individual's qualified relation for the month have each filed a return of income under this Act
-- for the applicable base taxation year."
GIVEN `resident in Ontario at the beginning of the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an eligible individual under ITA 122.5 (1) and not excluded by 122.5 (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `returns filed for the base taxation year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is eligible for the Ontario sales tax credit` IF
        `resident in Ontario at the beginning of the month`
    AND `an eligible individual under ITA 122.5 (1) and not excluded by 122.5 (2)`
    AND `returns filed for the base taxation year`

-- The s 103.8 (3) amounts that s 23 (3.3) indexes: $260 a person, the $20,000 single threshold, the $25,000 family one.
DECLARE `OSTC amounts` HAS
    `amount per person`       IS A NUMBER
    `single threshold`        IS A NUMBER
    `family threshold`        IS A NUMBER

`the OSTC amounts written in the Act` MEANS
    `OSTC amounts` WITH
        `amount per person` IS 260
        `single threshold`  IS 20000
        `family threshold`  IS 25000

-- s 103.8 (3): "(A – [0.04 × (B – C)])/12". "A": $260 for the individual; $260 for a qualified relation; $260 where there
-- is no qualified relation and the individual claims the s 118 (1) (b) (eligible dependant) amount for a qualified
-- dependant; $260 for each other qualified dependant -- so $260 for the individual and for each relation and dependant.
-- "B" the greater of the threshold and adjusted income; "C" the threshold: $20,000 with neither relation nor dependant,
-- $25,000 otherwise. "the amount, if any" (s 103.8 (1)): never below nil.
GIVEN `ostc` IS AN `OSTC amounts`
      `has a qualified relation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `qualified dependants` IS A NUMBER
      `adjusted income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 103.8 (3) monthly amount` MEANS
    LET `persons` MEANS 1 PLUS (IF `has a qualified relation` THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS `qualified dependants`
        `threshold` MEANS IF `has a qualified relation` OR `qualified dependants` GREATER THAN 0
                          THEN `ostc`'s `family threshold`
                          ELSE `ostc`'s `single threshold`
        `A` MEANS (`ostc`'s `amount per person`) TIMES `persons`
        `reduction` MEANS 0.04 TIMES ((max `threshold` `adjusted income`) MINUS `threshold`)
    IN  (`the excess of` `A` `over` `reduction`) DIVIDED BY 12

-- s 103.8 (4): a shared-custody parent gets "(D + E)/2", E computed as if not eligible for the shared-custody dependants.
GIVEN `ostc` IS AN `OSTC amounts`
      `eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has a qualified relation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `qualified dependants` IS A NUMBER
      `of whom in shared custody` IS A NUMBER
      `adjusted income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Ontario sales tax credit for the month` MEANS
    IF (NOT `eligible`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE LET `d` MEANS `the s 103.8 (3) monthly amount` `ostc` `has a qualified relation` `qualified dependants` `adjusted income`
             `e` MEANS `the s 103.8 (3) monthly amount` `ostc` `has a qualified relation` (`qualified dependants` MINUS `of whom in shared custody`) `adjusted income`
         IN  IF `of whom in shared custody` GREATER THAN 0
             THEN (`d` PLUS `e`) DIVIDED BY 2
             ELSE `d`

§§ `s 104 (8), (9) -- repaying an Ontario child benefit overpaid`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the individual`
    `the Ontario Minister`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `repay the excess Ontario child benefit to the Ontario Minister`
    `pay the March 15 instalment`
    `pay the June 15 instalment`
    `pay the September 15 instalment`
    `pay the December 15 instalment`

-- s 104 (8): if the individual "received an Ontario child benefit to which he or she is not entitled or received an amount
-- greater than the amount to which he or she is entitled, the individual shall repay the amount or the excess amount".
-- s 104 (9): (8) "does not apply if the total amount that is repayable ... for any 12-month period that commences on July 1
-- in a year is not more than $2". No time is set.
GIVEN `amount received for the 12-month period` IS A NUMBER, `amount entitled to for the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Ontario child benefit repayment is required` IF
    (`the excess of` `amount received for the 12-month period` `over` `amount entitled to for the period`) GREATER THAN 2

GIVEN `amount received for the 12-month period` IS A NUMBER, `amount entitled to for the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Ontario child benefit to repay` MEANS
    IF `an Ontario child benefit repayment is required` `amount received for the 12-month period` `amount entitled to for the period`
    THEN `the excess of` `amount received for the 12-month period` `over` `amount entitled to for the period`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `amount received for the 12-month period` IS A NUMBER, `amount entitled to for the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to repay an Ontario child benefit overpaid` MEANS
    IF `an Ontario child benefit repayment is required` `amount received for the 12-month period` `amount entitled to for the period`
    THEN PARTY `the individual`
         MUST  `repay the excess Ontario child benefit to the Ontario Minister`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED
